From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hoang Viet Pham <hoang.pham@adtran.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: npu: fix oversized WLAN mailbox message length

airoha_npu_wlan_msg_send() and airoha_npu_wlan_msg_get() compute the
mailbox message length as sizeof(*wlan_data) + data_len. struct
wlan_mbox_data ends in a union whose largest member is
u8 stats[WLAN_MAX_STATS_SIZE] (4408 bytes), used only by the stats-dump
command. Because that union sits after the DECLARE_FLEX_ARRAY(u8, d)
member, sizeof(*wlan_data) always accounts for the largest union
member, so every ordinary WLAN SET/GET message (band0_oncpu, tx-bufid,
pkt, tx-pkt, ba, force_to_cpu, ...) computes len == 4416 + data_len.

__airoha_npu_send_msg() rejects any len > AIROHA_NPU_MBOX_SIZE (256,
matching the size of the coherent bounce buffer allocated per core),
so every one of these WLAN mailbox commands returns -EINVAL before
ever touching the mailbox registers. On EN7581 boards this makes
airoha_npu_wlan_init_memory() fail unconditionally during mt76_npu_init(),
so NPU WLAN offload never comes up and wifi traffic never gets PPE
hardware acceleration, even though the NPU firmware loaded fine and
mt76_npu_check_ppe()/airoha_ppe_get_dev() succeeded.

Use offsetof(struct wlan_mbox_data, d) instead of sizeof(*wlan_data)
so the computed length only covers the fixed header plus the actual
payload being sent, not the trailing stats union.

Found and verified on SmartRG SDG-8716v (Airoha AN7581 + MediaTek
MT7992), where every airoha_npu_wlan_msg_send() call was failing with
len=4420, err=-22, blocking NPU WLAN offload entirely.

Signed-off-by: Hoang Viet Pham <hoang.pham@adtran.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
@@ -381,7 +381,7 @@ int airoha_npu_wlan_msg_send(struct air
 	struct wlan_mbox_data *wlan_data;
 	int err, len;

-	len = sizeof(*wlan_data) + data_len;
+	len = offsetof(struct wlan_mbox_data, d) + data_len;
 	wlan_data = kzalloc(len, gfp);
 	if (!wlan_data)
 		return -ENOMEM;
@@ -404,7 +410,7 @@ int airoha_npu_wlan_msg_get(struct airo
 	struct wlan_mbox_data *wlan_data;
 	int err, len;

-	len = sizeof(*wlan_data) + data_len;
+	len = offsetof(struct wlan_mbox_data, d) + data_len;
 	wlan_data = kzalloc(len, gfp);
 	if (!wlan_data)
 		return -ENOMEM;
